+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a duration string into a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. It accepts either a whole
+number of seconds made only of ASCII digits (such as `120`), or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups with the units
+`d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes) and `s` (seconds). Each unit may appear at most once and must appear in that
+order, with no spaces. Units are case-insensitive. Negative numbers, decimals and empty strings are rejected. A
+`timedelta` passed in is returned unchanged.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--wait", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def cli(wait):
+        click.echo(f"{wait.total_seconds():.0f} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(cli, args=['--wait=90m'])
+    invoke(cli, args=['--wait=1H30M'])
+    invoke(cli, args=['--wait=1h30'])
+```
+
